    "label": "Answer the Saved examples page",
    "job": "Answer the Saved examples page: list my saved examples, save one from its link, remove one",
    "description": "The Saved examples page's routes (GET /saved-examples lists every example newest first with its count; POST /saved-examples saves one from { url, title?, words?, pictures?, why_it_worked?, collection?, added_from? }, filling what was not given from the public link itself the first time; POST /saved-examples/remove { id } removes one). Each example is one saved-example record. The records it reads are the ones handed in as stored.records; the records it makes are handed back in keep (a removed example as a null value), and the run writes nothing itself. Answers { status, body } as the old account route did: a refused save is 400 with { error }, and the example stays as it was.",
